Why: four WAVE521C defects in upstream wave5-hw.c. (1) The sec-AXI size
accounting is a mainline TODO: only WAVE515 computes the line-buffer sizes, so
on WAVE521C the driver enables sec-AXI into the 64 KiB SRAM with zero sizes
(USE_SEC_AXI=0x8201), corrupting the write-back; forced to 0 (what the vendor
writes). (2) With two decode instances sharing the one VCPU, the DEC_PIC done
interrupt can precede the result becoming readable and the query returns
WAVE5_SYSERR_RESULT_NOT_READY; upstream fails the picture, this retries the
query. (3) wave5_vpu_enc_register_framebuffer's error path frees its local
vpu_buf copies while the same dma handles were already published into
p_enc_info->vb_*; wave5_vpu_enc_close() then frees them a second time
(observed live as 4x WARN in __dma_release_from_coherent when the vb_task
allocation ENOMEMs). Free the p_enc_info copies instead so the free memsets
the field close() looks at. (4) wave5_vpu_build_up_enc_param declares the one
device-global 64 KiB sec-AXI SRAM window to every encoder instance at
CREATE_INSTANCE, so two concurrent instances are handed completely
overlapping scratch; the vendor never declares a sec-AXI window to an encoder
instance, so the two writes are dropped.

Live encoder parameter changes. wave5_vpu_enc_change_param() issues
W5_ENC_SET_PARAM with OPT_CHANGE_PARAM so a running instance can change its
target bitrate, frame rate, VBV window and intra period without a
STREAMOFF/STREAMON cycle. The firmware leaves one report on the instance report
queue for that command, exactly as the seq-init path does, and it must be drained
with a GET_RESULT query: left there it sits ahead of every later ENC_PIC report,
finish_encode consumes it instead of its own frame, and the instance stalls after
the first change.

The change-mask bits are the vendor's (Wave5VpuEncParaChange): bit 1 intra
parameters, bit 6 frame rate, bit 8 target rate, bit 9 rate-control parameters.
The RC_PARAM write composes the whole word from current state rather than only
the three fields the vendor rewrites, because a partial word reads as
rc_enable = 0. Forcing a keyframe uses bit 1 with intra_period 1 for a single
picture; the per-picture W5_CMD_ENC_PIC_PIC_PARAM force-picture-type route was
swept across every plausible field layout on this firmware and produced no IDR.

